    "question": {
      ":question/id": "61bbcb11-a041-5904-99b3-0554eb9f6731",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y+z &=-1 \\\\ y-2z &=3 \\\\ -5x+15y-5z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 15 & -5 & 5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 15 & -5 & 5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. This gives,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
