    "question": {
      ":question/id": "93b3b475-b4b8-5ab1-8cc2-d72050854be1",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 3 y - 6 z &=-13 \\\\ y + 2 z &=3 \\\\ - 5 x + 15 y + 30 z &=65\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -6 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 15 & 30 & 65\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nFirst reduce the matrix to row echelon form, making each pivot equal to $1$.\n\n$$\nR_{3}:=R_{3}+\\left(5\\right)R_{1}\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -6 & -13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only.\n\n$$\nR_{1}:=R_{1}+\\left(3\\right)R_{2}\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
