    "question": {
      ":question/id": "87e3cd59-ede1-5d17-b4b3-f24903213b17",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - z &=3 \\\\ - x + 3 y - 5 z &=-12 \\\\ - 2 x + 2 z &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -5 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 & -6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nFirst reduce the matrix to row echelon form, making each pivot equal to $1$.\n\n$$\nR_{2}:=R_{2}+\\left(1\\right)R_{1}\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 & -9 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 2 & -6\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_{3}:=R_{3}+\\left(2\\right)R_{1}\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_{2}:=\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)R_{2}\\qquad M\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nIn the row echelon form above, we have only two pivots (in the $1$st and $2$nd columns). To transform the matrix to reduced row echelon form, we need to create zeros above the pivots only. The entry above the second pivot is already zero, so this is already reduced row echelon form.\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n",
